===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{n-g|An expression of surprise or disbelief.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|text='''What''', have his daughters brought him to this pass?}}
#: '''''What'''! [[that's|That’s]] [[amazing]]!''
# What do you want? {{non-gloss|An abrupt, usually unfriendly enquiry as to what a person desires.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''What'''? I'm busy.}}
# {{lb|en|British|colloquial|dated}} {{clipping of|en|what do you say|nodot=a}}? {{n-g|Used as a type of [[tag question]] to emphasise a statement and invite agreement, often rhetorically.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Denis Garstin|title=The Shilling Soldiers|year=1918|url=https://archive.org/stream/shillingsoldiers00gars|location=London|publisher=Hodder and Stoughton|page=83|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/shillingsoldiers00gars/page/83/mode/1up|text=“That’s riled them,” said my compaion. “Good work, '''what'''?”}}
#* {{quote-text|en|date=May 12 1991|chapter=[[w:List of Jeeves and Wooster episodes|Kidnapped!]]|title=w:Jeeves and Wooster|section=Series 2, Episode 5
|passage=''Chuffy:'' WHAT? No, no, no, no, no. My casa is your casa, '''what'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|It’s a nice day, '''what'''?}}
# What did you say? [[I beg your pardon]]? {{non-gloss|This usage is often considered impolite, with the more polite "[[pardon|Pardon]]?" or "[[excuse me|Excuse me]]?" preferred.}}
#: {{ux|en|— Could I have some of those aarrrrrr mmmm ...<br>— '''What'''?}}
# {{n-g|Indicating a guess or approximation, or a pause to try to recall information.}}
#: {{ux|en|I must have been, '''what''', about five years old.}}

